---
import type {RevisedCapability} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import {prototypeApproval} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import PentaInnerHero from './PentaInnerHero.astro';
import CapabilityReference from './CapabilityReference.astro';
import CapabilityEvidence from './CapabilityEvidence.astro';
import CapabilityInquiry from './CapabilityInquiry.astro';
import {libraryGuide} from '../data/resourceLibrary';
import '../styles/prototype-machining.css';
interface Props {page:RevisedCapability;quoteHref:string}
const {page,quoteHref}=Astro.props;
const cooling={...page.parts[1],text:'Intake and cooling interfaces for prototype fit checks. Define joints and any supplied-part scope.'};
const throttle={...page.parts[2],text:'Bores, mounting and actuator interfaces for development checks.'};
const materialLinks=[['Aluminum','aluminum-cnc-parts'],['Stainless steel','stainless-steel-cnc-parts'],['Copper & brass','copper-brass-cnc-parts'],['Engineering plastics','plastic-machined-parts']];
---
<div class="prototype-page pn-capability-rollout" data-penta-capability={page.slug}>
 <PentaInnerHero title={page.plan.title} lead="Covers, housings and custom parts for fit, assembly and design evaluation. Machined to an agreed revision, with the checks needed for your next decision." slug={page.slug} part={page.parts[0]} quoteHref={quoteHref} secondaryHref="#part-examples" secondaryLabel="Define the evaluation"/>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-scope" id="part-examples" data-core-section="evaluation-scope"><header><h2>Define what the prototype must answer</h2><p>We plan the prototype around the question it needs to answer: fit, assembly, appearance or a defined functional check. Mark fixed interfaces, mounting datums, clearances and cover fits on the drawing.</p></header><div class="prototype-references"><CapabilityReference part={cooling} namedLink singleEntry/><CapabilityReference part={throttle} namedLink singleEntry/></div><div class="prototype-application"><h3>Automotive &amp; motorcycle prototypes</h3><div><p>Specify pressure, functional or vehicle tests separately from machining. Include the procedures, fixtures, acceptance limits and responsibility for validation.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-approval" id="engineering-fit" data-core-section="approval-record"><header><h2>Keep the revision, checks and approval together</h2></header><table class="rd-table rd-stacked"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">Method & responsibility</th><th scope="col">Reviewable result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{prototypeApproval.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.stage}</th><td data-label="Input">{row.input}</td><td data-label="Method & responsibility">{row.method}</td><td data-label="Reviewable result">{row.result}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><div class="prototype-approval-evidence pi-inspection-pair"><CapabilityEvidence id="cmm-room" caption="Original LZZ CMM photograph." sizes="(max-width:767px) calc(100vw - 90px), 400px"/><div><h3>Define the prototype checks</h3><p>Agree the measurement method, current calibration and report scope for the prototype; this is not its inspection result.</p><a class="rd-link" href={libraryGuide('machined-prototype-approval-checklist').href}>Prototype approval checklist</a></div></div></section>
 <section class="prototype-section prototype-differences" id="materials-finishes" data-core-section="production-differences"><header><h2>Record what differs from production</h2><p>A prototype may use the intended production material, condition and finish, or an approved alternative for the evaluation. Record where the alternative limits conclusions about the production part.</p></header><dl><div><dt>Material and condition</dt><dd>Record any change in alloy, temper, polymer grade, fillers or stock condition. Aluminum options include 6061 and 7075, subject to review of the temper, evaluation requirements and intended production specification. Confirm heat treatment and required material records.</dd></div><div><dt>Finish and working surfaces</dt><dd>Define the prototype finish and intended production treatment. Protect working fits, contact areas, threads and dimensions after treatment.</dd></div><div><dt>Edges and measurement state</dt><dd>Agree burr limits, edge quality, cleaning and measurement conditions. Where the prototype uses a substitute material or finish, identify the application checks that require the production specification.</dd></div></dl><nav class="prototype-material-links" aria-label="Material selection">{materialLinks.map(([title,slug])=><a class="rd-link" href={'/capabilities/'+slug+'/'}>{title}</a>)}</nav><div class="prototype-next"><h3>The next revision or batch</h3><div><p>Record feedback, open issues and permitted changes. Identify and approve the next model / drawing revision before another prototype is machined. Keep acceptance tied to the tested revision and evaluation scope; agree the batch baseline, quantity, sampling and commercial order before repeat production.</p><nav aria-label="Next production steps"><a class="rd-link" href="/capabilities/low-volume-production/">Plan the first batch</a><a class="rd-link" href="/about/how-we-work/">Project responsibilities</a></nav></div></div></section>
 <CapabilityInquiry page={page} quoteHref={quoteHref} title="Request a prototype review" orderFirst coreSection="quotation"/>
</div>
